# Frontend Rules — Cursor Leaderboard

These rules apply to **all frontend/UI code** in the cursor-leaderboard project, including:
- Generated HTML (TV display)
- Realtime WebSocket overlay logic
- Phone camera capture page

This project intentionally uses **Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS** only.

---

## 1. Tech Stack (Non-Negotiable)
- Vanilla HTML
- Vanilla CSS
- Vanilla JavaScript
- No frameworks (❌ React, ❌ Vue, ❌ Angular)
- No bundlers or build steps
- One-file output preferred for TV (`leaderboard.html`)

---

## 2. Core Design Principles
- Generated HTML must be **self-contained**
- UI must work in:
  - Chrome
  - Safari
  - TV browsers
- No runtime dependencies except:
  - Browser APIs
  - WebSocket
- Readability > cleverness

---

## 3. Generated HTML Rules (TV)
- All logic must be embedded via `<script>`
- Avoid global namespace pollution
- Wrap logic in IIFEs
- Never hardcode WebSocket URLs
  - Must resolve dynamically via:
    1. `?ws=` query param
    2. `window.LEADERBOARD_WS_URL`
    3. fallback default
- DOM updates only (no reloads)

---

## 4. Slider / Overlay Rules
- Slider state is **in-memory**
- Slides must:
  - Appear immediately
  - Auto-remove after timeout
- Duplicate detection must be prevented:
  - Same email within cooldown → ignore
- Queue must be FIFO
- Never block the main slideshow

---

## 5. Unknown / Error UI Handling
- Always reuse the **same slide frame**
- Unknown user:
  - Shorter display duration
  - Clear “User not found” messaging
- Data missing:
  - Show name + image
  - Replace metrics with “Data not found”
- UI must never appear broken or empty

---

## 6. Phone Camera Page Rules
- Camera must auto-start (no buttons)
- Use `getUserMedia` safely:
  - Handle unsupported browsers gracefully
- Capture logic:
  - Delay before first frame
  - Throttled frame sending
- Never spam backend
- Show only preview (no UI clutter)

---

## 7. Performance Rules
- Avoid expensive DOM operations in loops
- Use `requestAnimationFrame` when animating
- Avoid layout thrashing
- Cleanup timers and listeners

---

## 8. Security Rules
- Never expose secrets in JS
- Do not trust WebSocket payload blindly
- Sanitize injected text
- Restrict dynamic file paths

---

## 9. Documentation Requirement (Mandatory)
Every UI change must include:
- Update to relevant `.md` doc:
  - `face-detection.md`
  - `api-reference.md`
  - or `architecture.md`
- Explanation of:
  - What changed
  - Why it changed
  - Any UX impact

---

## 10. Commit Message Rules
- feat(frontend): add live queue preview on TV slide
- fix(frontend): delay camera capture to avoid unknown detection
- perf(frontend): reduce DOM updates in overlay
- docs(frontend): update face-detection flow


---

## 11. AI Prompting Rule
When using AI:
- Always ask for:
  - Browser compatibility check
  - Runtime behavior explanation
  - Failure/edge cases
- Output must be copy-paste runnable
